# I04.var05 v1.0.1 recovery design draft 1: NO_GO

The first prospective recovery contract was generated without invoking SIMLOX. It is preserved as `i04-var05-prospective-recovery-v101-20261008.json` (85,505 bytes, SHA-256 `f21fa274af1eba21986ba4072c9a5dce2a7a6ca53c2ca769d55f0efc32ed6547`) with generator `i04-var05-recovery-design-v101-20261008.py`. The original generator capture receipt is `i04-var05-recovery-contract-proof-v101-20261008-01/receipt.json` (941 bytes, SHA-256 `9d4feca86f5946c8919160823db9c992488c2100726d1edf63caf1a998ab337e`); its actual exit was integer zero and original stderr was empty.

This draft omits the three actual zero-native SSH preflight transport originals in `cases/simlox-air-support/I04-var05-zero-transport-between-v1.0.0/transport-evidence/ssh-preflight-20261008T082059090580Z-4a07f5a8/`. Its `frozen_v100_preflight_originals` list contains 15 receipt/helper/root-wrapper files, but that category did not include the separate transport receipt, stdout, and stderr. It also omitted the original guard stdout/stderr in the root failure-seal directory and the author PURE copier's captured stdout/stderr. The corrected contract must pin these bytes distinctly without treating the first draft as launch approval.

The frozen v100 source inventory, manifest, preflight approval, failed run, root failure seal, and independent NO_GO remain unchanged. No v1.0.1 case package, canonical manifest, SSH preflight, or native run exists from this draft.
